        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "40c8a64b-1cbd-5797-908c-3b9311ffd949",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier, Trevor Bayne\n- Companies: Ford, Go FAS Racing, Roush Fenway Racing\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Ford Mustang, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan\n- Events: 1997 CART season\n- Concepts: Rookie of the Year, NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series, NASCAR Xfinity Series, CD3 platform\n- Places: Hermosillo\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier was the Rookie of the Year in the 1997 CART season.\n- The Ford Fusion was introduced for the 2006 model year.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant alongside the Lincoln MKZ, and it was formerly produced alongside the discontinued Mercury Milan.\n- The Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, and Mercury Milan share the CD3 platform.\n- Patrick Carpentier currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.\n- Trevor Bayne currently competes full-time in the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series, driving the No. 6 Ford Fusion for Roush Fenway Racing.\n- Trevor Bayne currently also competes part-time in the NASCAR Xfinity Series, driving the No. 60 Ford Mustang for Roush Fenway Racing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9d57f489-229a-5831-91af-bfe46bc6e876",
        "text": "Page: Patrick Carpentier. Sentence: Patrick Carpentier (born August 13, 1971) is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\nPage: Patrick Carpentier. Sentence: He currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.\nPage: Ford Fusion (Americas). Sentence: Introduced for model year 2006, the Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant along with its rebadged variant the Lincoln MKZ — and formerly with its now discontinued rebadged variant, the Mercury Milan, all sharing the CD3 platform.\nPage: 1997 CART season. Sentence: Rookie of the Year was Patrick Carpentier.\nPage: Trevor Bayne. Sentence: He currently competes full-time in the Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series, driving the No. 6 Ford Fusion for Roush Fenway Racing and part-time in the NASCAR Xfinity Series, driving the No. 60 Ford Mustang for RFR.",
